#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198099 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d40cb0df-fce7-5236-b0ef-62f5a343b3a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12724" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](images/0c/0c81e18633c3089e7c9f56464738a57dae490c70a0c8b46d116b1a8d75cd433f.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](images/0a/0a76866dfc078172503784c3d67c7d36abbfe3362a9af3e07e6055f168debbf4.svg)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198100 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "3e2319b4-ab10-50ef-845b-9586c9761227" :question/math-academy-id "e-12725" :question/problem "Consider the following compound predicate:\n\n$x$ is positive **and** a multiple of $4,$ **or** $x$ is negative.\n\nExpress this compound predicate in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $M(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $4$\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is positive and a multiple of $4.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{is positive}}_P \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{and}}_{\\land} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is a multiple of }4 }_M,\n$$\n\nthat is, $P \\land M.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is negative. This corresponds to $N.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x \\,\\textrm{ is positive}\\,\\textrm{and a multiple of }4 }_{P \\land M} \\quad \\underbrace{\\vphantom{p}\\textrm{or}}_{\\lor} \\quad \\underbrace{x \\vphantom{p}\\textrm{ is negative} }_N,\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P \\land M) \\lor N.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198101 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/id #uuid "3a115dd5-3241-5627-bb40-121b75eeb7ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-12726" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}{:}$\n\n- $P(x):$ $3x -1 < 5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x \\geq 3$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P(x) \\lor Q(x)$ represents the *union* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{P \\lor Q} = T_P \\cup T_Q\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x){:}$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n$T_P = (-\\infty,2).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n$T_Q = [3,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P∨Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,2)\\cup [3,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198104 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/id #uuid "2ab89571-f4e2-515f-9d01-b1213e73ffc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12733" :question/problem "Write a sentence that is equivalent to the following: \"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is negative and it is an integer.\"" :question/worked-solution "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"$x$ is negative and it is an integer\" with the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and it is negative.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and $x$ is an integer and it is negative.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$x$ is an integer and $x$ is an integer\" to just \"$x$ is an integer\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is an integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"$x$ is a negative integer.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41dde3e3-6092-50d7-a3e3-9b03129714b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381363} {:answer/id #uuid "ab38e2e3-7aa0-5681-bd79-b716a1f5ebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨(P∧Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381364} {:answer/id #uuid "765bffbf-d84a-5ff5-a5f8-870a92ad58fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381365} {:answer/id #uuid "63cf5e8f-593a-5960-b49a-27fd32e7eff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(Q∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381366} {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b83a791-8241-5cd5-855b-476449665c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381367} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22e7a73-f4cf-5a91-83ba-e94d101da87b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ff7b2b7-dfb5-55b1-bfd4-172f42c8239c" :question/math-academy-id "q-170725" :question/problem "$x$ is even **or** odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is odd" :question/worked-solution "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71006df3-094b-544a-8d16-aac2cd8f3223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∨G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389658} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad243f-0f35-5ec2-8ec0-8002c544b1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∧G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389659} {:answer/id #uuid "8c521dcf-8c85-5590-bbe0-f4ea54692826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∧(G∧F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389660} {:answer/id #uuid "dc23a41f-2a8c-5280-8a84-ec9e53692ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(F∧G)∨(F∧G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389661} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb348b5-55ca-5bc3-a13c-7902825b88c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∧(F∨G)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9ad243f-0f35-5ec2-8ec0-8002c544b1cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F∧G" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389659} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d3a206-f750-5622-89b6-8d0f7fa111af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "017fc845-8be5-5798-b79f-7d6c9b39bc09" :question/math-academy-id "q-170730" :question/problem "$x$ is divisible by $2$ **and** $3.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $F(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $2$\n\n- $G(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $3$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is divisible by }2}_{⏟}}_{F}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is divisible by }3}_{⏟}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $F∧G.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce659c55-ca26-52c6-b15e-ec317013d856" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Nested Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a506dcfe-4cec-5d6a-92b6-e01253a0c863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(O∧E)∧(N∧P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194779} {:answer/id #uuid "ce08a6b9-09b8-5a85-9e1f-70b6689cbee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(O∨E)∧(N∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194780} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0ba6e6-ac14-5c01-ab04-354cad316027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(O∨E)∨(N∨P)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194781} {:answer/id #uuid "409e2007-9a38-5696-9da9-eaeaf9f1209d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((O∧E)∧N)∧P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194782} {:answer/id #uuid "6f748e69-8c13-524b-bfe8-82199f40cd15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((O∨E)∧N)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194783}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f941fb41-1019-5d5f-b49a-6f151680cdc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194778}] :question/id #uuid "e6d7fc87-c9d5-5ec1-9313-97840cdea5be" :question/math-academy-id "q-170743" :question/problem "> $x$ is odd **or** even, **and** $x$ is negative **or** positive.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $O(x)$: $x$ is odd\n- $E(x)$: $x$ is even\n- $N(y)$: $y$ is negative\n- $P(y)$: $y$ is positive"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5dce47e-44d3-5a2b-8197-8bc58ccfa8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is odd or prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381391} {:answer/id #uuid "927712c1-5e63-55f4-b93d-ce9a38637890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is odd or prime but not both." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381392} {:answer/id #uuid "b24ed5bb-b839-5d04-9f01-99bfbc097da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is odd." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381393} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5492ea-f705-5e32-8c74-2af730823972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381394} {:answer/id #uuid "fad267b6-504e-5fd0-b9ce-01ef1a3a6d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is odd and prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5dce47e-44d3-5a2b-8197-8bc58ccfa8f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x$ is odd or prime." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381391} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7fa6fd1-c852-5ca2-8111-31391b68c5a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9f9ef807-17a8-5045-81d3-1c4bb492856b" :question/math-academy-id "q-171041" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: \"$x$ is odd and it is an odd number, or $x$ is odd or it is a prime number.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd and it is an odd number\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or $x$ is odd or it is a prime number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$x$ is odd or $x$ is odd\" to just \"$x$ is odd.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$x$ is odd, or it is a prime number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$x$ is odd or prime.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2993b4ab-e45b-579a-8a11-b5e9ee107d5b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791ba16d-0fde-5494-ae38-151cf6473679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧(P∨Q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381497} {:answer/id #uuid "570ac923-c70f-5b05-85ab-6d0e3179805a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∧Q)∨P" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381498} {:answer/id #uuid "26713a16-ca66-5149-b579-24b29515572c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(P∨Q)∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381499} {:answer/id #uuid "814273a2-7641-537c-b209-0d0278585880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381500} {:answer/id #uuid "87001085-7898-5d47-97c2-c648e169d76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∨Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "814273a2-7641-537c-b209-0d0278585880" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P∧Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381500} :answer-field/id #uuid "56d3c014-7399-5320-a01a-ad25e78491d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8a305e0-7087-5ce5-b288-8389af590e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-175349" :question/problem "$x$ is a multiple of $3$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $3$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5$" :question/worked-solution "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is a multiple of }3}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6bc626a-9517-584c-bf55-8653227f830e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Truth Sets of Conjunctions and Disjunctions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e396ea68-6feb-5cd5-8ac6-e75dc6c53bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/405bfcc79e29a36adaea9d397f6d33794daababc01025e0f9fd4183016398007.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381581} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2f451a-abba-58cf-ba36-3980aed2aa22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/43/4338f5eb43d21bf87798fdb325176ebdaa29b6ced4a32d0699f235e47aa96504.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381582} {:answer/id #uuid "8c37fdef-89a8-55f1-a500-1d50f6f2da5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/725d8e0dd8392861882f4a73f7cb44fddd93e0835248c7050518b2cb0a4c6098.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381583} {:answer/id #uuid "eb26620f-271d-553e-b738-1bab29737e7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b663a4b3b3108b7d85cb2817d96ed4e6e7b8feb547d8f78882ec4596a57087ff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381584} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8f3ab4-2286-5108-ba03-20d92a6e351e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09ccd14aa66859f0e61997975c6c5ea4d760d4b575236533079289036728b821.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f8f3ab4-2286-5108-ba03-20d92a6e351e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/09/09ccd14aa66859f0e61997975c6c5ea4d760d4b575236533079289036728b821.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381585} :answer-field/id #uuid "245e5abb-d683-5a1d-9ee6-964c287d4d18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ddcaadb-b673-5ff3-867c-10c08e9772d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177730" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b444409245ad52ba5bafe15f8ca354f2daa7caea3e0c5fb46e4d71a62dcf66d7.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of the predicates $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P∧Q?$" :question/worked-solution "The truth set of $P∧Q$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P∧Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x,y)∨Q(x,y),$ we take all the points that belong to both ${T}_{P}$ and ${T}_{Q},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/09ccd14aa66859f0e61997975c6c5ea4d760d4b575236533079289036728b821.png)\n\n**Note:** The points where the *dashed* line segment meets the *solid* curve do not belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$, since these points are *not* in  ${T}_{Q}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f674fcf-7f3e-53c0-8759-6f83b0820160" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Conjunction and Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46192eea-f4ae-5745-ab2b-1935f29c22a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive but not both" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426815} {:answer/id #uuid "9046c2c1-c0ee-5e13-92fe-5436918ed8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426821} {:answer/id #uuid "91799f63-a171-5d71-abd6-d2ac6eb622bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426822} {:answer/id #uuid "a892fa0b-ae64-5844-bb4e-4a9d0eb3ece7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational and positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426826} {:answer/id #uuid "c455468d-3494-592f-8fea-f7eb970fc2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9046c2c1-c0ee-5e13-92fe-5436918ed8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$z$ is rational or positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426821} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4aac9d-4227-5875-926d-41c64f7175cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be776820-4de7-562d-ad85-1f2cc185142d" :question/math-academy-id "q-177759" :question/problem "Simplify the following sentence: \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational and it is a rational number\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or $z$ is rational or it is a positive number.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"$z$ is rational or $z$ is rational\" to just \"$z$ is rational.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$z$ is rational, or it is a positive number.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"$z$ is rational or positive.\""}]}
